SCORING A
1. typeScore[t] = sum of question weight shares (Section 2.5) for tags t. digCount = sum of shares for DIG (cap 3).
2. specScore = 2 × typeScore[primary] + typeScore[secondary] + (digital = yes ? digCount : 0) + follow-up points (+3 per selected follow-up option).
3. Ranking by specScore descending; ties by catalog order.
4. Primary = rank 1. Alternative = highest-ranked specialization whose primary type differs from Primary's primary type. Stretch = highest-ranked specialization whose primary type differs from both. Explain on screen: "Alternative and Stretch come from different work styles so you can compare."
5. Archetype = highest typeScore (ties: order AN, ST, BU, PE, CO, OP). Blend per Section 3.3.
6. Strength labels for the "Your pattern" bars (not percentages): rank 1 and 2 of the six types = "Strong", ranks 3 and 4 = "Moderate", ranks 5 and 6 = "Light". Add a note: "This shows relative preference, not ability."
7. "Is an MBA right now?" note (show up to two sentences, first matches win):
 - If the reasons contain only EXPECT and/or UNSURE: "Your reasons are still forming. Talk to three MBA graduates before you commit."
 - If XP0: "Programs differ: some are built for freshers and others prefer work experience. Check the class profile of your target colleges."
 - If SWITCH: "Career switchers do best with an internship or project in the new field. Plan one early."
 - If BIZ: "Check whether the program has an incubator or a venture track."
