SCORING D
- Dimension score = Σ(points × weight × calibration) ÷ Σ(weight × calibration) over answered, scored questions in that dimension. Not-sure answers (non-K) are excluded; the dimension is marked "Partly assessed". If a dimension has no scored answers it is "Not assessed" and excluded from the overall score.
- Calibration multiplier: FRESHER: ROLE and EVID questions × 1.5. INTERN: EVID questions × 1.5. LATERAL: EVID questions × 1.5. All others × 1.
- Overall weights (normalise over assessed dimensions):
 FRESHER: ROLE 18, EVID 18, TECH 18, PRACT 14, NET 8, POS 14, AIF 10
 INTERN:  ROLE 10, EVID 24, TECH 18, PRACT 14, NET 8, POS 16, AIF 10
 LATERAL: ROLE 8,  EVID 28, TECH 18, PRACT 14, NET 8, POS 14, AIF 10
- Status per dimension: Ready 70 and above; Close 50 to 69; Gap below 50. Overall: 70 and above "Interview-ready"; 50 to 69 "Close: targeted prep needed"; below 50 "Not yet: build the foundation first". Round to the nearest whole number.
- Be honest. Do not soften a Gap. For every Gap or Close, name the specific action that closes it (Section 7 plan action library).
