90-DAY PLAN
- Ask (with defaults) for three weekly practice slots (default Mon, Wed, Fri evening) from a fixed choice list. Write every action as "If it is <slot>, then <action>".
- Build from the 3 lowest assessed dimensions. Normal mode: Weeks 1 to 4 Foundation (lowest two dimensions), Weeks 5 to 8 Practice, Weeks 9 to 12 Apply and refine. Sprint mode (D-AD4): Weeks 1 to 2 Foundation, Weeks 3 to 4 Practice, Weeks 5 to 12 Apply and maintain, with weekly numeric targets × 1.5 (rounded up).
- Every week has one measurable output and a tick box. Show a progress count ("5 of 12 weeks done"). Tick state is kept in memory only.
- Action library (resource types only; never invent named sources):
 ROLE: read 3 real job descriptions and list the 5 most repeated tasks; talk to 1 person in the role; write a one-page "a week in this role" note and get it checked by that person.
 EVID: PM: write a mini product requirement document for an app you use. SC: solve and write up one full case. IB: build a simple DCF and comparables sheet for a listed company. Generic: complete one work sample for the role. INTERN: ask your manager to let you own one deliverable and request written feedback. LATERAL: write 3 impact stories with numbers. If PROJ_IDEAS: list 3 project ideas for the role.
 TECH: PM: 3 product-sense drills and 2 metrics drills a week. SC: 3 cases a week plus 15 minutes of daily mental math. IB: 4 accounting and valuation sessions a week plus one deal summary a week. Generic: answer 20 core role questions aloud, timed.
 PRACT: 1 mock interview a week (Foundation), 2 a week (Practice and Apply); record, review, log one fix per mock.
 NET: send 5 outreach messages a week; book 2 calls a week; ask each person for one referral or one next contact.
 POS: tailor the resume with 3 quantified bullets; write a 60-second pitch; write a "why this role, why now" story; get a peer review.
 AIF: use an AI tool on one real task a week and write down what you checked and what it got wrong; build one small piece of work using AI and be ready to explain how you verified it.
